        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7df97f7e-6fde-51d9-a82f-6887425b0177",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Andrew Macdonald, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Beach, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle, T2 Trainspotting, Porno, 28 Days Later\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, producer, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge, born in 1964, is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- Andrew Macdonald, born in 1966, is a Scottish film producer.\n- John Hodge is most noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel \"Trainspotting\" into the screenplay for the 1996 film \"Trainspotting.\"\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"Shallow Grave\" in 1994.\n- Andrew Macdonald collaborated with John Hodge and director Danny Boyle on \"Shallow Grave\" in 1994.\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"Trainspotting\" in 1996.\n- The 2000 film \"The Beach\" is a British-American adventure drama directed by Danny Boyle and adapted for film by John Hodge from Alex Garland's 1996 novel of the same name.\n- John Hodge wrote \"A Life Less Ordinary\" in 1997.\n- John Hodge wrote \"The Beach\" in 2000.\n- Andrew Macdonald collaborated with John Hodge and Danny Boyle on \"The Beach\" in 2000.\n- John Hodge wrote \"The Final Curtain\" and the short film \"Alien Love Triangle\" in 2002.\n- Andrew Macdonald collaborated with John Hodge and Danny Boyle on \"28 Days Later\" in 2002.\n- \"T2 Trainspotting\" was directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge, based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in the novels \"Trainspotting\" and \"Porno.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "80cc64cf-1e22-58ca-8c45-c58507d9cc9f",
        "text": "Page: John Hodge (screenwriter). Sentence: John Hodge (born 1964) is a British screenwriter and dramatist, most noted for his adaptation of Irvine Welsh's novel \"Trainspotting\" into the script for the film of the same title.\nPage: John Hodge (screenwriter). Sentence: His films include \"Shallow Grave\" (1994), \"Trainspotting\" (1996) \"A Life Less Ordinary\" (1997), \"The Beach\" (2000), \"The Final Curtain\" (2002), and the short film \"Alien Love Triangle\" (2002).\nPage: The Beach (film). Sentence: The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle and based on the 1996 novel of the same name by Alex Garland, which was adapted for the film by John Hodge.\nPage: T2 Trainspotting. Sentence: The film is directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge, based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in his novel \"Trainspotting\" and its follow-up \"Porno\".\nPage: Andrew Macdonald (producer). Sentence: Andrew Macdonald (born 1966) is a Scottish film producer, best known for his collaborations with screenwriter John Hodge and director Danny Boyle, including \"Shallow Grave\" (1994), \"Trainspotting\" (1996), \"The Beach\" (2000) and \"28 Days Later\" (2002).",
